From: Armada Linux <armada@localhost>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: include attributes in INIT_CREATE_ATTR scalars

The user-PD creation code fills six input arguments. The plain INIT_CREATE
method uses the first four, but INIT_CREATE_ATTR also needs the attributes
and signature length in arguments four and five. Advertising only four
input buffers drops both arguments from the payload. Match the six-buffer
wire format used by the SM6150 CDSP firmware.
---
 drivers/misc/fastrpc.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1623,9 +1623,11 @@ static int fastrpc_init_create_process(struct fastrpc_user *fl,
 	args[5].length = sizeof(inbuf.siglen);
 	args[5].fd = -1;
 
-	sc = FASTRPC_SCALARS(FASTRPC_RMID_INIT_CREATE, 4, 0);
-	if (init.attrs)
-		sc = FASTRPC_SCALARS(FASTRPC_RMID_INIT_CREATE_ATTR, 4, 0);
+	if (init.attrs)
+		sc = FASTRPC_SCALARS(FASTRPC_RMID_INIT_CREATE_ATTR,
+				    FASTRPC_CREATE_PROCESS_NARGS, 0);
+	else
+		sc = FASTRPC_SCALARS(FASTRPC_RMID_INIT_CREATE, 4, 0);
 
 	err = fastrpc_internal_invoke(fl, true, FASTRPC_INIT_HANDLE,
 				      sc, args);
-- 
